# fixedbugs, defect 2467, lane b31-ffi, 2026-11-11: `own.h` declares
# `f2467(int, int)` and defines `f2467` as a macro of one argument. The
# declaration gives two and its result is right; the call goes through the
# macro, which takes fewer, and is told so. Until this defect: *returns `int
# (int, int)`*; this line is its mark.
extern "own.h"
    function f2467(a: i32, b: i32) -> i32  #~ ffi_macro_name

function main()
    print(f2467(a: 1, b: 2))
